Requires: \fBsuperuser\fR.
.RE
.\" END GENERATED: command user verify
.TP
.B "user scope " \fIname\fR " " [ "list " | " add " \fIs\fR[,s...] | " remove " \fIs\fR[,s...] | " replace " \fIs\fR[,s...] | " remove \-\-all" ]
Manage which scopes
.I name
can authenticate from. This is a membership list: a user with no scopes
can authenticate nowhere. With no subcommand (or
.BR list ),
prints the user's current scopes with orphan detection (any scope
name that does not resolve to an existing scope is flagged red).
.B add
and
.B remove
accept one or a comma-separated list of existing scope names;
.B replace
replaces the whole list;
.B "remove \-\-all"
empties it (with confirmation) and takes no scope names.
.B "remove \-\-all"
preserves the bcrypt hash — distinct from
.B user disable
in that intent is "temporarily revoke scope access" rather than
"revoke the password".
