test the change first: log in as
.B "host enroll"
and
.B "host sync"
do (the invoking user's ssh, agent, port and key), check that the login is
root or may use sudo (sudo that asks for a password is refused without a
terminal), read the host's ssh keys over that session and compare them with
the pinned ones (another key refuses the change, with both fingerprint sets:
the host must be the same machine), and record the address reached. A
provisioning login that is a user of tacctl is refused, as at enrollment. Only
